{
  "metadata": {
    "schema_version": 4,
    "name": "odum-gnp-loop",
    "description": "Phase D.1 \u2014 money as a closed, conserved GNP loop (Odum Fig. 3). The C.4 countercurrent drained money one way into a sink, so the 'conserved: true' declaration on the money carrier asserted nothing: conservation is measured over STORAGE nodes only, and a source/sink pair contributes none. Here money circulates households -> exchange -> firms -> households with no money source and no money sink, so the total is a real invariant the solver must hold. Energy over the same run is NOT conserved \u2014 it dissipates to heat and to the consumed sink \u2014 which is the asymmetry Odum draws: energy flows through, money goes round."
  },
